From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:48:05 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 32/95] Plutonium: unit tests for the broker and grant checks

EXO-BROKER: plutonium_unittests (chrome/test/BUILD.gn), a target of its
own on //chrome/browser and content's test support, about 800 build
steps from a built chrome against about 8,800 for unit_tests:
- exo_window_broker_unittest.cc: grants (issue, resolve, validate,
  forged tokens, other frames and pages), revocation (explicit, window
  close, navigation, reload; back/forward-cached documents keep theirs),
  a new document in the same RenderFrameHost (RenderDocument for main
  frames off), and observers' events not nesting.
- plutonium_shell_unittest.cc: IsShellDocument (other origins,
  about:blank, iframes, error pages, prerendered, fenced frames, inner
  contents, back/forward cache), the WindowBroker binder, grantrevoked
  forwarding (this document's grants only), resubscribing, and
  NativeWindowHost.Attach refusals told apart by their log lines, plus an
  unattached host given Focus/SetSize/... over raw Mojo (what a
  compromised renderer can send).
ExoWindowBroker::AddWindowForTesting() stands in for Exo's windows.

content_unittests: RenderWidgetHostInputEventRouterTest covers
IsForeignFrameSinkEmbeddedHere() and RouteToForeign()'s check, with a
fake ForeignFrameSinkDelegate.

Run with --ozone-platform=headless.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
